By Law of Cosines on triangles $AFP$ and $BCQ$, we get $AP^2=FP \cdot d_a=df$ and $BQ^2=CQ \cdot d_b=d_bc$, respectively.
Adding, we get $AP^2+BQ^2=(FP+d_a)(CQ+d_b)=AB^2$.
