Similarly, we can find that $\frac{CK}{\sin 2 \theta}=CD = BD = BC = AB = \sqrt{(10^2 + 25^2 - 15^2)}$.
Then using $\sin 2(\frac{\pi}{3}-\frac{1}{2} \alpha) = \frac{\cos \alpha -\sin^2\alpha}{2\cos \alpha}$, we get $\frac{65^2}{53^2} = \frac{-\cos \alpha}{1+\sin^2 \alpha} = \frac{BC^2}{54^2}$.
